==Pre-match==

===Identity===
The original identity of the 2023 UEFA Europa League Final was unveiled at the group stage draw on 26 August 2022.<ref>{{cite news |date=26 August 2022 |title=2023 UEFA Europa League and 2023 UEFA Europa Conference League finals identities unveiled {{!}} Inside UEFA |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0278-15f5454ff2ca-671989a3cb07-1000--2023-uefa-europa-league-and-2023-uefa-europa-conference-league-/ |access-date=26 August 2022 |website=[[UEFA]]}}</ref>

===Ambassador===
The ambassador for the final was former Hungarian international [[Zoltán Gera]], who finished as runner-up in the [[2009–10 UEFA Europa League]] with [[Fulham F.C.|Fulham]].

===Ticketing===
With a stadium capacity of 63,000 for the final, a total amount of 46,800 tickets were available to fans and the general public, with the two finalist teams receiving 15,000 tickets each, and with the other tickets being available for sale to fans worldwide via ''UEFA.com'' from 21 to 28 April 2023 in four price categories: €150, €100, €65, and €40. Accessibility tickets for disabled spectators cost €40. The remaining tickets were allocated to the local organising committee, national associations, commercial partners, and broadcasters, and to serve the corporate hospitality programme.<ref>{{cite news |title=Ticket sales for 2023 UEFA club competition finals launched |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0280-17d41ec484ee-05fcab4e5d9d-1000--ticket-sales-for-2023-uefa-club-competition-finals-launched/ |website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=21 April 2023}}</ref>

==Match==
===Summary===
In the 35th  minute, Roma went in front when [[Paulo Dybala]] slotted the ball low into the right corner of the net after a pass from [[Gianluca Mancini]], but Sevilla equalised ten minutes into the second half when Mancini turned the ball into his own goal after a cross from [[Jesús Navas]] on the right to make it 1–1. The game went to a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalties]] following almost 132 minutes of game time. After two missed Roma penalties in the shootout, one of which was saved by goalkeeper [[Yassine Bounou]] and the other of which hit the post, [[Gonzalo Montiel]], who also scored the winning penalty for [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] in the [[2022 FIFA World Cup final]] against [[France national football team|France]], scored the winner for Sevilla. His penalty at first was missed but was re-taken owing to encroachment.<ref name="CriticalResponse1">{{cite news |title=Sevilla 1–1 Roma (4–1 on penalties): Spanish side make history as Mourinho throws medal into crowd |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/65770780 |access-date=1 June 2023 |newspaper=BBC Sport}}</ref>

